1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,490
This is the implementation demo for journey five.

2
00:00:03,490 --> 00:00:07,700
It is the real application and API running on this machine,

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:11,340
with a synthetic buyer and a local payment adapter.

4
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:14,830
No real card is used and nothing is ever charged.

5
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:17,780
The buyer opens the Pay step.

6
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:22,940
The order and the price come from the server: fifty dollars for a first inspection.

7
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:28,160
A card number with too few digits, a bad expiry and no security code is refused with

8
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:29,520
a list of what to fix.

9
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:33,750
A test card that the bank declines shows that the card was declined,

10
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:37,540
says nothing was charged, and offers to add a different card.

11
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:42,630
A card that works pays, and the page confirms the amount and the last four digits.

12
00:00:42,630 --> 00:00:47,100
The receipt appears in billing history, described as a first inspection.

13
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:52,200
And the next vehicle is cheaper: with both reviews it comes to forty five dollars.

14
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:55,140
Payments are safe to repeat.

15
00:00:55,140 --> 00:01:00,200
Creating the same checkout twice, with the same key, returns the same checkout.

16
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:05,130
Five payment requests sent at the very same moment all return the same single

17
00:01:05,130 --> 00:01:07,560
payment, and the card is charged once.

18
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:12,880
The browser sends card details only to the payment processor and gets back a token,

19
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:18,070
so the card number never reaches our API, and we keep only the brand and the last

20
00:01:18,070 --> 00:01:18,840
four digits.

21
00:01:19,990 --> 00:01:23,890
The refund rules are in place for the booking journeys to use.

22
00:01:23,890 --> 00:01:28,980
A seller who does not show, or an inspection that cannot finish, refunds in full.

23
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:32,940
Cancelling more than two hours before the call refunds in full,

24
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:36,210
and cancelling later keeps a twenty five dollar fee.

25
00:01:36,210 --> 00:01:39,420
A report that has been delivered is not refundable.

26
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:42,380
These rules are covered by the automated tests.

27
00:01:43,530 --> 00:01:45,450
Here is what to remember.

28
00:01:45,450 --> 00:01:47,830
The server decides every price.

29
00:01:47,830 --> 00:01:52,370
A payment goes through once, however many times it is sent.

30
00:01:52,370 --> 00:01:55,290
Card details never touch our database.

31
00:01:55,290 --> 00:01:58,600
Next, journey six: book a video inspection.
